    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied, the server defaults it to today, and the value round-trips as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges, each in its proper place:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's both an editable request field and part of the response DTO. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` column (`registration_date`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column. hsqldb drives the tests; the others are updated for consistency.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** (new function) \u2014 a single-responsibility step that sets `LocalDate.now()` only when the built owner has no registration date, leaving a supplied date untouched.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `build` and `save`, under the existing `transaction` governance.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name (both sides `LocalDate`), so no mapper change was needed \u2014 the defaulting is the only new logic, and it lives in its own small class rather than being folded into an existing step.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
